## What a real version would need

| Feature we faked or skipped | Why a real company would need it | How hard / expensive? |
|---|---|---|
| Real accounts and logins | Students must manage only their own listings and requests, and verifying a student email would keep it to real students | Easy to medium: a SaaS login service, cheap at small scale but more as it grows |
| Mobile app | Students are always on their phones | Expensive: needs a developer and a platform |
| Notifications | Email or text alerts for new requests, due dates and other messages | Medium: a SaaS email/SMS service, with a cost per message |
| Hosting for the site and app | It needs to stay online, especially at the start of semesters when people are buying textbooks | Medium: a PaaS hosting platform, with cost rising as traffic increases |
| Data security and privacy | The site would hold names, student emails, payment details and pickup locations | Hard and expensive: a PaaS with built-in security tools like encryption and access controls, and it's not a one-time purchase |

